  "description": "PIBYEH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C216 H304 Co4 N8 O30 Y4. From the CIF bond table, Y1 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Y3 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Y4 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.188-4.928 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.13-174.82°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C216H308Co4Y4N8O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
